  },
  {
   "id": "samp17",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -230,
   "y": -47,
   "width": 460,
   "height": 66,
   "text": "**sample** x_D ~ softmax per position    \nand keep **argmax** x̂",
   "color": "#e879f9"
  },
  {
   "id": "xd18",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -20,
   "y": 59,
   "width": 40,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl19",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 170,
   "y": 47,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`x_D, x̂, entropy H [256]`"
  },
  {
   "id": "acc20",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -230,
   "y": 108,
   "width": 460,
   "height": 96,
   "text": "**accept (entropy bound)** — sort positions by H, take the k lowest while ΣH − max H ≤ 0.1; they get their sample x_D",
   "color": "#e879f9"
  },
  {
   "id": "ren21",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -230,
   "y": 244,
   "width": 460,
   "height": 66,
   "text": "**renoise** — every other position ← a fresh uniform random id",
   "color": "#f59e0b"
  },
  {
   "id": "nc22",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -20,
   "y": 350,
   "width": 40,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl23",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 170,
   "y": 338,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`next canvas [256]`"
  },
  {
   "id": "done24",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -230,
   "y": 399,
   "width": 460,
   "height": 76,
   "text": "**done?** x̂ unchanged for 1 step and mean H < 0.005,    \nor 48 steps used",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "commit25",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -230,
   "y": 515,
   "width": 460,
   "height": 96,
   "text": "**yes → commit x̂** (the argmax canvas, not the sample) · ids after an EOS → pad · stop on EOS, else next canvas",
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "loop-r1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1660,
   "y": 407,
   "width": 260,
   "height": 60,
   "text": "**no → next step**    \nwhole decoder pass again",
   "color": "#f59e0b"
  },
  {
   "id": "loop-r2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1660,
   "y": -1745,
   "width": 260,
   "height": 60,
   "text": "↻ **denoising step**    \nnew canvas in",
   "color": "#f59e0b"
  },
  {
   "id": "loop-s1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1310,
   "y": -150,
   "width": 240,
   "height": 60,
   "text": "processed logits → next step",
   "color": "#22c55e"
  },
  {
   "id": "loop-s2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1310,
   "y": -1408,
   "width": 240,
   "height": 60,
   "text": "self-conditioning input",
   "color": "#22c55e"
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-mask",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 630,
   "y": -1301,
   "width": 620,
   "height": 100,
   "text": "**Who attends to whom** — rows = queries, columns = keys. Prefix = prompt + finished canvases (in the KV cache)."
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-mrow0",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 630,
   "y": -1145,
   "width": 110,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "**encoder**"
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-mcol0",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 750,
   "y": -945,
   "width": 110,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "prefix"
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-mrow1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 630,
   "y": -1027,
   "width": 110,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "**decoder**"
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-mcol1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 868,
   "y": -945,
   "width": 110,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "canvas"
  },
  {
   "id": "mk00",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 750,
   "y": -1181,
   "width": 110,
   "height": 110,
   "text": "causal ◣",
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "mk01",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 868,
   "y": -1181,
   "width": 110,
   "height": 110,
   "text": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "mk10",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 750,
   "y": -1063,
   "width": 110,
   "height": 110,
   "text": "all ✓",
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "mk11",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 868,
   "y": -1063,
   "width": 110,
   "height": 110,
   "text": "all ↔",
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-mask",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 630,
   "y": -895,
   "width": 620,
   "height": 220,
   "text": "Encoder: causal; image tokens also see their whole image (`use_bidirectional_attention = \"vision\"`, sliding layers). Decoder: `is_causal = False` — every canvas position sees the cached prefix and the whole canvas, incl. positions to its right. Sliding layers keep only the last 1024 prefix tokens in the cache; global layers see all of it. The decoder never writes the cache."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-layers",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 630,
   "y": -645,
   "width": 620,
   "height": 190,
   "text": "Per layer: attention 34.6M (sliding) / 49.0M (global) · dense MLP 17.8M · router 0.4M · 128 experts 761.3M (5.9M each, SwiGLU-style 2816→704→2816, GELU-tanh).    \nPattern: [5 sliding, 1 global] × 5. Context 262,144 positions."
  },
  {
   "id": "raw26",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1460,
   "y": -1760,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**prompt** — chat template text, `<image>` placeholders",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "tok27",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1400,
   "y": -1664,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**tokenizer** (vocab 262,144)",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "pids28",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1270,
   "y": -1568,
   "width": 40,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl29",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1860,
   "y": -1580,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`prompt ids [P]`"
  },
  {
   "id": "pemb30",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1400,
   "y": -1519,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**embed** (same table) × √d",
   "color": "6"
  },
  {
   "id": "pe31",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1363,
   "y": -1423,
   "width": 225,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl32",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1080,
   "y": -1435,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`[P, 2816]`"
  },
  {
   "id": "splice33",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1460,
   "y": -1374,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**splice**: each image's placeholders ← its 280 soft tokens",
   "color": "#a78bfa"
  },
  {
   "id": "px34",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1363,
   "y": -1278,
   "width": 225,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl35",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1860,
   "y": -1290,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`x [P, 2816]`"
  },
  {
   "id": "enc36",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1460,
   "y": -1229,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 96,
   "text": "**encoder pass** — the same 30 layers, run **once**, causal; no self-conditioning, no lm head",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "kv37",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1460,
   "y": -1093,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 116,
   "text": "**KV cache**, per layer    \nsliding: K, V 8 × 256 for the last 1024 tokens    \nglobal: K (= V) 2 × 512 for every token",
   "color": "5"
  },
  {
   "id": "reenc",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1460,
   "y": 515,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 96,
   "text": "**encoder pass over the 256 committed ids** (causal, same layers) appends their K, V",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "img38",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -2450,
   "y": -2048,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**image** → 16×16 patches",
   "color": "#a78bfa"
  },
  {
   "id": "patch39",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -2480,
   "y": -1952,
   "width": 360,
   "height": 76,
   "text": "**patch embed** 768 → 1152 + 2-D position table  \n24.5M",
   "color": "#a78bfa"
  },
  {
   "id": "vp40",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -2346,
   "y": -1836,
   "width": 92,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl41",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -2910,
   "y": -1848,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`[patches, 1152]`"
  },
  {
   "id": "vit42",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -2480,
   "y": -1787,
   "width": 360,
   "height": 76,
   "text": "**ViT × 27** · 16 heads × 72 · MLP 4304  \n545.1M",
   "color": "#a78bfa"
  },
  {
   "id": "pool43",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -2450,
   "y": -1671,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**pool 3×3** · standardize",
   "color": "#a78bfa"
  },
  {
   "id": "evis44",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -2450,
   "y": -1575,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 66,
   "text": "**embed_vision** RMSNorm → 1152 → 2816  \n3.2M",
   "color": "#a78bfa"
  },
  {
   "id": "vt45",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -2413,
   "y": -1469,
   "width": 225,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl46",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -2910,
   "y": -1481,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`soft tokens [280, 2816] per image`"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-vis",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -2600,
   "y": -1400,
   "width": 600,
   "height": 150,
   "text": "Gemma 4 vision tower (572.8M). 280 soft tokens per image by default; the card lists budgets of 70 / 140 / 280 / 560 / 1120. Runs once per image, inside the encoder pass only."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-eb",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1060,
   "y": -12,
   "width": 700,
   "height": 230,
   "text": "**Nothing is frozen inside a canvas.** The accept set is recomputed every step from fresh logits; a position not accepted this step is re-randomised even if it was accepted before. The canvas settles because the model grows confident, and only x̂ of the last step is kept. Generation config: up to 48 steps, `max_new_tokens` 256 (= 1 canvas), EOS ids [1, 106, 50]."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-card",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1060,
   "y": 248,
   "width": 700,
   "height": 130,
   "text": "Model card: 15–20 tokens per forward pass on average, i.e. a 256-token canvas typically takes ~13–17 decoder passes instead of 256 autoregressive ones. The decoder also multiplies the tied table twice per position (lm head and soft embedding)."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-llada",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1300,
   "y": 695,
   "width": 1400,
   "height": 300,
   "text": "**vs. LLaDA2.2-mini** (also a diffusion MoE, see that model)  \n- Noise: LLaDA starts a block as `<|mask|>` tokens and fills masks (masked diffusion); DiffusionGemma starts from **uniform random ids** and re-randomises rejected positions (uniform-noise diffusion).\n- Block: LLaDA 32 tokens, one stack with a block-causal mask and no KV cache; here 256 tokens, an **encoder pass** caches the prefix once and a bidirectional **decoder pass** reuses the same weights.\n- Committing: LLaDA writes a mask when p > 0.5 and keeps it (rewrites / deletes via T2T edits); here an **entropy-bound** set is accepted per step, nothing is frozen, and the canvas ends on stability + confidence (48 steps max).\n- Extra: self-conditioning on the previous step's logits; LLaDA has none. LLaDA routes experts per 32-token block; here plain per-token top-8."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-src",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 200,
   "y": 695,
   "width": 1300,
   "height": 300,
   "text": "**Sources.** config.json, generation_config.json and the safetensors headers of google/diffusiongemma-26B-A4B-it (1047 tensors, all BF16) — stored total **25.82B** (25.25B without the vision tower; card: 25.2B), active **3.84B** (card: 3.8B). Dataflow from transformers' diffusion_gemma (DiffusionGemmaForBlockDiffusion, EntropyBoundSampler, StableAndConfidentStoppingCriteria). The text encoder stores only 30 `layer_scalar` values; all its other weights are tied to the decoder (`_tied_weights_keys`). The repo also ships a diffusers BlockRefinementScheduler config (block 32, 32 steps, threshold 0.95); transformers' `generate()` does not use it."
  }
 ],
